# Target credentials: each is independently optional; configure one per provider your tickets use.
# Both set = one invocation serves mixed-provider tickets; neither set = the run fails at startup.
# SSH authorization for clone and push stays independent of these REST publication credentials.

# GitHub work (git@github.com:<owner>/<repository>.git tickets)
# Fine-grained GitHub personal access token with Metadata: Read and Pull requests: Write on the ticket repository.
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# Azure DevOps work (git@ssh.dev.azure.com:v3/<organization>/<project>/<repository> tickets)
# PAT scope: Code (Read & write)
AZURE_DEVOPS_PAT=

# Backlog: the private GitHub repository whose issues are the tickets, and the Project v2 board whose
# Status field owns lifecycle. Required for every runner and submission invocation.
# Classic personal access token (fine-grained tokens cannot reach Projects v2) with the `repo` scope
# for the private issues and the `project` scope for the board.
# Paste the board address from the browser: https://github.com/orgs/<owner>/projects/<number> for an
# organization project, https://github.com/users/<owner>/projects/<number> for a personal one. A link to a
# specific view (.../views/<number>) is accepted. This setting replaces FORGE_BACKLOG_PROJECT_ID; the raw
# node id is no longer read, and the runner resolves the URL to that id once at startup.
FORGE_BACKLOG_REPOSITORY=
FORGE_BACKLOG_PROJECT_URL=
FORGE_BACKLOG_TOKEN=
